3.0 Developers:  Some More Last Minute Suggestions

As somewhat of a neophyte among hackers (I haven't solved Nethack
yet), I am a little hesitant to make suggestions for 3.0, especially
since it appears that they would be too late.  However, I am a 
little curious as to how people would react to them.

1) With regards to pets, how about making f(elines) available as an
   alternative or lower-level improvement to d(ogs)?  Fog clouds 
   have never seemed to be a very important monster0type; f(elines)
   could be made faster (4 attacks/round) and smarter than dogs
   (never getting underfoot, being more finicky as to what they eat,
   etc).  They could become available at a lower level in 
2) The Pet Shop.  After seeing David's Treasure Zoo and the effects
   of Charm monster and leashed Floating Eyes, I wondered if it
   would be possible to "buy" tame/loyal monster-pets and pet-type 
   accessories like leashes, pet-toys, cat-nip, etc.

3) Archeologists seem to me to be the weakest over-all characters
   in nethack.  One of their more useless and encumbering tools is
   the large box.  Maybe it would be possible to replace the heavy
   box with a lighter implement which could serve a similar purpose,
   like a cooking kit or bunsen burner.  For that matter, has anyone
   given thought to including pieces of wood or other flamable 
   material in the dungeons to start or build fires with?         
   Archeologists could be given lighters initially ("You flick your
   Bic").

4) Or maybe it is time to introduce a new character type:  the 
   Alchemist.  He/she could be equipped with a lab-kit, several
   potions (identified), a bunsen-burner, a lab-coat (AC 10),
   special goggles, tongs, gloves, mirror, empty test-tubes,
   powdered chemicals, water, wielding a beaker of acid (40 +
   throws), and the #examine command.  He/she would have the
   ability to actually create potions or combine/transform them.
   There could be potions of polymorph which brings me to 

5)  a #polymorph command.  Why isn't there a way to #polymorph
   oneself, once one has a ring of polymorph control?  Also, why
   not have intrinsic polymorph if one eats a dead shape-changer
   or is bitten by one(vampire bites (in either direction) could
   give one a semi-permanent polymorph to vampire).

Anyway, these are just some suggestions.  Feel free to comment.
